            <div xml:id="d845">

                <pb facs="1062" n="963" xml:id="pg963"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">611.3131/71: Telegram</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Acting Secretary of State to the Chargé in
                        Venezuela</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic">Villard</hi>)</head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Washington</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1936-12-31T18:00:00-05:00">December 31, 1936—6
                        p.m.</date></dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>57. Your despatch No. 549, December 22. The Department authorizes you to inform
                    the Venezuelan Foreign Minister orally and informally that this Government is
                    now prepared to enter into preliminary conversations looking towards the
                    conclusion of a reciprocal trade agreement as soon as the Venezuelan Government
                    removes the existing discrimination against American commerce. You should
                    qualify this statement, however, by saying that this Government before
                    discussing possible schedules desires to limit the conversations to discussions
                    of the general provisions of the agreement in order to ascertain whether the two
                    Governments are in accord with respect to these. You should add that this
                    Government desires that no publicity be given to such conversations, it being
                    the intention of this Government to make a public announcement at an appropriate
                    time in accordance with its customary procedure if a mutually satisfactory basis
                    for an agreement is found.</p>
                <p>Please keep the Department informed on developments by telegraph.</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Moore</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
